1) Chief complaint & onset → “failing health” due to loss of perceived telepathy, 8 months ago;  
2) Course → gradual, weather-sensitive;  
3) Associated symptoms → denied constitutional, neurological, cognitive, or psychiatric symptoms beyond distress and disconnection;  
4) Past medical history → none;  
5) Medications/allergies → only Peruvian herbs, no allergies;  
6) Social/occupational/exposure → lives alone, works in health food store, impaired sense of self;  
7) Targeted physical examination → thyroid appearance uncertain (but TSH normal), insight assessed and preserved;  
8) Laboratory/imaging → TSH normal; other labs unavailable, but clinical picture does not suggest acute organic illness.  

No domain is missing. The evidence is complete and sufficient to conclude the presentation is not driven by acute or progressive organic disease, psychosis, or major mood disorder with delusions — but rather a distressing, insight-preserved shift in self-perception and environmental attunement. All eight domains have been systematically covered.

